  "title": "Lotus Temple, Delhi",
  "summary": "The Lotus Temple is a Bahá'í House of Worship in New Delhi, designed by the Iranian architect Fariborz Sahba. Its flowerlike form uses 27 marble-clad petals set in clusters of three. It was dedicated in December 1986 and is open to people of any religion.",
